---
import App from "../layouts/App.astro";
import roadmap from "../data/roadmap.json";
const { nodes, phases, scale, asOf, target } = roadmap;
const core = nodes.filter((n) => n.core);
const pct = (v) => `${(v / 4) * 100}%`;
const today = new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-CA", { timeZone: "Asia/Kuala_Lumpur" });
const phaseNow = phases.find((p) => today >= p.from && today <= p.to);
const daysLeft = Math.max(0, Math.ceil((new Date(target).getTime() - new Date(today).getTime()) / 86400000));
---
<App title="Progress" description="Twenty skills, rated 0 to 4. Where I started, where I am, where I'm going.">
  <h1>Progress</h1>
  <p class="muted small mono">Rated {asOf} · target 31 Dec 2026 · {daysLeft} days left{phaseNow && <> · now: <strong>{phaseNow.name}</strong> (weeks {phaseNow.weeks})</>}</p>

  <h2>The four that fix the gig</h2>
  <p>Lead lines hit other strings, fingers slow, guitar unheard. Not a theory problem. These four nodes are the whole job until they’re at 3.</p>
  {core.map((n) => (
    <div class="node core">
      <div class="head"><span>{n.id}. {n.name}</span><span class="r">{n.now} → {n.goal}</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><i class="base" style={`width:${pct(n.baseline)}`}></i><i class="now" style={`width:${pct(n.now)}`}></i><b class="goal" style={`left:${pct(n.goal)}`}></b></div>
      <div class="gate small muted">gate: {n.gate}</div>
    </div>
  ))}

  <h2>Scale</h2>
  <ol start="0" class="small">{scale.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ol>

  <h2>All twenty</h2>
  {nodes.map((n) => (
    <div class="node">
      <div class="head"><span>{n.id}. {n.name}</span><span class="r">{n.now} → {n.goal}</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><i class="base" style={`width:${pct(n.baseline)}`}></i><i class="now" style={`width:${pct(n.now)}`}></i><b class="goal" style={`left:${pct(n.goal)}`}></b></div>
      <div class="gate small muted">{n.gate}</div>
    </div>
  ))}
  <p class="small muted">Bar: faint = where I started, gold = now, tick = goal for 31 Dec.</p>

  <h2>Phases</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Weeks</th><th>Phase</th><th>Nodes</th><th>Result the band hears</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{phases.map((p) => <tr class={p === phaseNow ? "on" : ""}><td>{p.weeks}</td><td>{p.name}</td><td>{p.nodes.join(", ")}</td><td>{p.outcome}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Why this order</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>5 and 6 first.</strong> The lead lines fail because other strings ring and the picking is uneven. Two weeks of muting and metronome picking and the same lines come out clean.</li>
    <li><strong>7 and 8 next.</strong> Same notes on different strings, and dynamics from the hands. The fastest way for an electric to get heard without playing more.</li>
    <li><strong>9 to 12 after.</strong> One pentatonic box rooted properly, then bends. A clean fill with one in-tune bend beats a fast sloppy run.</li>
    <li><strong>13 and 14 late.</strong> Swells and delay need muting and dynamics under them.</li>
    <li><strong>15 anytime.</strong> Nashville numbers are five minutes a day reading a chart as numbers. No guitar needed.</li>
    <li><strong>18 and 19 after 31 Dec.</strong> Scale theory stacked on a shaky pentatonic is the classic mistake.</li>
  </ul>
</App>
<style>
  .node{padding:12px 0 10px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .node.core{border-top-color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px}
  .head .r{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:var(--t-xs);color:var(--ink-soft);white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;padding-top:3px}
  .bar{position:relative;height:6px;background:var(--line);margin:8px 0 4px;overflow:visible}
  .bar i{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;height:100%}
  .bar .base{background:var(--ink-faint)}
  .bar .now{background:var(--accent)}
  .bar .goal{position:absolute;top:-4px;width:2px;height:14px;background:var(--ink);margin-left:-1px}
  .gate{margin-top:2px}
  tr.on td{background:var(--card)}
</style>
